# HTML Arcade Pinball — Build Plan

**Stack**: Single HTML file, Canvas 2D, vanilla JS. No build step, no dependencies.

## Core pieces
1. Table layout — canvas-drawn playfield: walls, slingshots, bumpers, flipper pivots, drain zone, launch lane.
2. Physics loop — ball as circle with position/velocity, gravity, wall collision (reflect + energy loss), circle-vs-line collision for flippers/walls.
3. Flippers — two rotating paddles, keyboard-controlled (left/right arrow or Z/X), impulse applied to ball on contact.
4. Bumpers/targets — circle bumpers that kick the ball on hit + add score; drop targets or lit rollovers for bonus.
5. Launch mechanism — spring-pull (hold spacebar, release = launch force) sending ball up the right lane.
6. Scoring/UI — score counter, ball count (3 balls per game), game over / tilt state.
7. Sound (optional) — simple WebAudio beeps on bumper hits.
8. Game loop — requestAnimationFrame, fixed-timestep physics update, render pass.

## Build order
1. Static table render (walls, flippers at rest).
2. Ball + gravity + wall bouncing, no flippers yet.
3. Flipper input + collision response.
4. Bumpers + scoring.
5. Launch lane + multi-ball lifecycle (drain → next ball → game over).
6. Polish: sounds, tilt, visual juice.
